      <memberdef kind="function" id="class_benchmark_1a8b4bab8a038fba5d18366ba23e32923f" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>juce::Result</type>
        <definition>juce::Result Benchmark::runEpoch</definition>
        <argsstring>()</argsstring>
        <name>runEpoch</name>
        <qualifiedname>Benchmark::runEpoch</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Runs one epoch. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>The function deletes the old samples file. It starts a <ref refid="class_sampler" kindref="compound">Sampler</ref> when the manifest has a <computeroutput>## sample</computeroutput> table. It launches <computeroutput>command manifest</computeroutput> in the manifest folder and waits until the command ends. It then drains the <ref refid="class_sampler" kindref="compound">Sampler</ref> and reads the samples file through <computeroutput><ref refid="class_benchmark_1ae59eaa6c1836391353180c17526f1c16" kindref="member">addEpoch</ref></computeroutput>. It adds the wall time of the epoch, in ns, to the <computeroutput>epoch</computeroutput> samples. On all systems it also adds the user and system time of the child, in ns, to the <computeroutput>user</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>system</computeroutput> samples. It last pads each row that has no sample in this epoch with zero.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="return"><para>Ok when all steps succeed. Otherwise the first failure: <computeroutput>\&lt;command path\&gt;: command failed</computeroutput> when the command does not exit with 0, the failure of the <ref refid="class_sampler" kindref="compound">Sampler</ref> when it cannot start, read or stop, or <computeroutput>not found: \&lt;samples path\&gt;</computeroutput> when the command writes no samples file. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
