      <memberdef kind="function" id="class_benchmark_1ac2758e9667d09cca4fa1c7d0845c7413" prot="public" static="no" const="yes" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>juce::ValueTree</type>
        <definition>juce::ValueTree Benchmark::getProfiles</definition>
        <argsstring>(const juce::ValueTree &amp;baseline) const</argsstring>
        <name>getProfiles</name>
        <qualifiedname>Benchmark::getProfiles</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>const juce::ValueTree &amp;</type>
          <declname>baseline</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Returns the profiles of all epochs. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>The tree holds one table for each table type, with one row for each zone. For each table type that holds bins, it also holds a table of the type <computeroutput>\&lt;TYPE\&gt;_CALLS</computeroutput>. That table has one row for each zone that holds bins, with the <computeroutput>percentile</computeroutput> property. Its statistics come from the merged bins of all epochs. The last table is the <computeroutput>run</computeroutput> table that the samples file holds. Each zone that the matching table of <computeroutput>baseline</computeroutput> also holds adds the comparison properties.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>baseline</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Tree of an earlier report. It may hold no matching table.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>Tree of the profile tables. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
